      "created_at": "2015-01-18T04:51:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The wording on this card is a little odd: \"Whenever a target is destroyed, put it under its associated deck\". Most cards elsewhere in the game refer to placing a card on the \"bottom\" of the deck. Other cards like Savage Mana use \"beneath\".</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>However, we didn't find any cards in the M.D.P. deck that suggested some other mechanic took effect, so we interpreted it to mean \"put the card on the bottom of the deck\". Thoughts? Is this just wording that could be tightened up?</span></p>",
